> His helpers aren't particularly threatening either, though watch out
> for giants picking up the boulders and freeing Sam.

That used to be my method of choice in the past, too. But it is not as
easy as you think. You have to be at high enough level yourself to hit
him with bullets, even if both your bullets and firearm are highly
enchanted. (Tried that out in wizard mode, too. Below approximately
level 23, you will not ever hit him.) So that method is not too useful
for a character that has not already gotten very far. If you *need* to
kill him, because his shop has the magic lamp that you need to get magic
resistance, then you cannot wait until you are level 25 or higher. (At
23, you may just hit him once every two rounds of seven bullets.) Well,
of course you can still try to steal items. The simplest way of killing
him as a low-level character seems to be to polymorph into a giant
shoggoth. The fight may become tight, if you do not have enough
intrinsic protection, as armor cannot be worn by a shoggoth.

